{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do","id":1245145,"title":"What can potions and ointments in 2e/ 3e do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-12T11:13:47-07:00","id":1245145,"title":"What can potions and ointments in 2e/ 3e do?","content":"It can't be an artifact.<br /> <br /> So yes, I was thinking of potions and ointments in exalted, and I was thinking of possible ones that could be made. So! A thread for that. <br /> <br /> Elixir of health<br /> Made from cow milk, ground up roots, and rare herbs from the West, this potion allows the imbibed to gain 1 dot of stamina, allowing the sickly to walk and making warriors to be in the peak of health. The effect wears off after 1 month, so it must be bought continuously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T20:31:55-07:00","id":1245303,"title":"","content":"I have allowed exceptionally crafted potions and ointments to work like exceptional tools for just about anything justified. Blade oils and performance drugs giving troops +1 to attack or movement, stimulants adding to perception/awareness, pastes to resist infections and concoctions to resist poison and disease...<br /> <br /> I've also let bigger crafts (major for something akin to a single dose, superior for large batches) edge near to what would usually be made via small sorcerous workings, albeit temporary instead of lasting.A single bountiful, disease free harvest, immunity to some diseases for a few months. The highest power I've allowed was &quot;For this battle this battle group has might 1&quot;. These stronger creations are almost always under first age craft, as they're disruptive enough on their own as to merit being a reclaimed treasure from a glorious past.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind...this is all arbitrary. These are the limits I set on my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T20:40:43-07:00","id":1245305,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's ok. <br /> <br /> As long as it's fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T05:28:15-07:00","id":1245410,"title":"","content":"Well, the people of Grieve have developed an elixir that makes them into a kind of weird vampire, although that's probably difficult to replicate.<br /> <br /> I feel as though a lot of potion things should be largely plot devices, or the process for some kinds of thaumaturgy and sorcerous working. An extra dot of Stamina both seems quite strong, and kind of too simple, and I think that would go for a number of ideas in which it gives you stat boosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T06:23:06-07:00","id":1245434,"title":"","content":"I've dabbled with rules for combat enhancing drugs based upon the rules for poison, in that the immediate effect is beneficial but you still suffer initiative damage each round that becomes actual damage in initiative crash. Though because it's mechanically problematic to give more than 1 non-charm dice at a time I found the best way to implement this was in the form of an artifact that dispensed the drug via Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T07:22:25-07:00","id":1245460,"title":"","content":"Oh, how about a drug that lets you ignore wound penalties and spend health levels to boost dice pools, which represents you &quot;overclocking&quot; your body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T07:41:07-07:00","id":1245469,"title":"","content":"If I were coming up with something for my group...<br /> <br /> A one-dot &quot;artifact&quot; of a potion represents some sort of major alchemy that has a single-Scene use and gives a sizeable bonus. Probably like a three-dot artifact give or take, but only once. They'd still be items of legend, singularly or as a class.<br /> <br /> A higher-dot &quot;artifact&quot; potion would be some sort of philosopher's stone or immortality serum or the like, that has long-lasting implications and is probably a macguffin. I might also allow a reusable bottle (tiny doses, regrows more as you go) as a regular Artifact, along the lines of the one-drop healing potion from Narnia - and with its own set of Evocations to boot.<br /> <br /> In both those cases, they would be a home-table interpretation for a player who wants to pursue an alchemy or herbalist theme. Neither would appear in-setting by default.<br /> <br /> A few dots' worth in a satchel of potions would be an equipment bonus on Medicine rolls, but not a distinct singular item on its own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T02:40:12-07:00","id":1245808,"title":"","content":"Well, you can initiate into sorcery daoist-style, with a life of temperance and an alchemical potion that purifies your essence. That's a pretty neat trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T00:47:08-07:00","id":1246905,"title":"","content":"OOoohhh.... I've been reading harry potter. Lots of ideas. How about liquid luck? How about potions that grant you resistance to fire for a day? What about ointments that instantly cure boils and cuts? What about potions that can make your hair grow longer, or you taller? <br /> <br /> Maybe basically the artifact zero version of hair dyes? All temporary, and all unnoticeable compared to exalted. But still useful for mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T02:29:40-07:00","id":1246925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do?p=1246905#post1246905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading harry potter. Lots of ideas. How about liquid luck? How about potions that grant you resistance to fire for a day? What about ointments that instantly cure boils and cuts? What about potions that can make your hair grow longer, or you taller?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me personally, potions in Harry Potter represent one of those instances in which the boundaries between magical items or products and the kind of magic that people can wield personally is kind of blurry...<br /> <br /> Wait, forget about all of that... I actually think that some of this may be on to something...<br /> <br /> I suddenly have an image of something like... a means to grant somebody benefits about equivalent to several kinds of Merit (possibly including some of the ones that you would get from sorcerous initiation) on a temporary basis.<br /> <br /> Something like Felix Felicis I would feel should be reserved for something on the level of a brew concocted by a high ranking divinity, but I could see a bunch of the rest working.<br /> <br /> Damn; good job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe basically the artifact zero version of hair dyes? All temporary, and all unnoticeable compared to exalted. But still useful for mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe, I was actually responding to this post ready to say something like &quot;why do you need a magic potion to change somebody's hair colour&quot;, but then I realised that you were using it as an analogy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:24:48-07:00","id":1246974,"title":"","content":"They don't need to be temporary. But, as is usual with these things, for PCs that includes a XP cost, serving more as a trainer tool than an actual power upgrade. This is compatible with your basic presentation idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:39:33-07:00","id":1246979,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'd allow somebody with Craft (Alchemy) and some Occult to whip up minor potions like that. You can probably find them for sale in most markets, next to the talismongers. Even the least of them (changing your hair color) is probably Resources 2, with Ointment of Proof Against Fire being a fair bit more.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't even say such things aren't useful to Exalts. Changing your height and making your hair three inches longer isn't impressive for a Night Caste Master of Disguise, but it's pretty useful for the Zenith who's being hunted for heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T20:26:48-07:00","id":1247277,"title":"","content":"Then what would resource 5 be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T23:21:34-07:00","id":1247291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do?p=1246974#post1246974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't need to be temporary. But, as is usual with these things, for PCs that includes a XP cost, serving more as a trainer tool than an actual power upgrade. This is compatible with your basic presentation idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if you do stuff like put it and sell it on the market? I mean, its not just for the PCs, its also for worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T04:48:08-07:00","id":1247346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do?p=1247277#post1247277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what would resource 5 be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still far below the effects of even minor artifacts, but..<br /> <br /> The very best Maiden Tea.<br /> <br /> A thick, gritty substance smeared onto the skin that grants 2 Lethal soak, but no Bashing, and imposes a -1 Mobility penalty. It hardens and stiffens your skin which makes you harder to cut, but not appreciably harder to crush, and your joints don't work as well as they ought until it wears off.<br /> <br /> A potion that vastly increases physical strength at the price of rapidly degrading the body. For the purposes of Feats of Strength, your Strength is increased by 2, but whenever you use these dice, you take an unsoakable llevel of Bashing damage. Users may experience casual strength problems as they accidentally crush fragile objects.<br /> <br /> An oily black tonic supposedly made from kraken blood filtered through the caul of a ghost-blooded infant. When imbibed, you become capable of breathing water, but incapable of breathing air, for the next hour. It sees surprisingly little use in underwater exploration,, but stands out as one of the most outrageously expensive poisons in Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T05:09:31-07:00","id":1247351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do?p=1246974#post1246974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't need to be temporary. But, as is usual with these things, for PCs that includes a XP cost, serving more as a trainer tool than an actual power upgrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels a bit pointless as something that is taking place at the resolution level of the mechanics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T16:08:17-07:00","id":1247535,"title":"","content":"So, in 2e, these are the substances the Art of Alchemy canonically covers making (#/# is degree/difficulty): <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Alchemical Touchstone (0/1; a general category of items, both stones and liquids, that can be used to identify a specific substance).</li> <li>Life's Little Luxury Blends (0/1; another general category, including deodorants, cleaning agents, dyes, trick powders that foam when put in alcohol or vinegar, etc).</li> <li>Blood-Staunching Compress (1/3; keeps wounds from re-opening).</li> <li>Draught of Blessed Respite (1/2; a sleeping potion that has a weird effect taken at a half-dose, allowing the character to act at high penalties while getting credit for sleeping).</li> <li>Eagle's Eye Potion (1/3; bonus die to vision-related Perception rolls, also versions for other senses).</li> <li>Hero's Recovery (1/3; potion that lets mortals heal as if they were Exalted).</li> <li>(Type) Venom-Allaying Draught (1/2; antitoxins, each specific to a poison).</li> <li>Wound-Cleansing Unguent (1/1; character doesn't have to make infection rolls after surgery).</li> <li>Age-Staving Cordial (2/3; as per the core rules).</li> <li>Ardent Embrace Resin (2/3; D&amp;D-style &quot;alchemist's fire&quot;)</li> <li>Final Vengeance (2/3; ignore pain, including wound penalties. Stamina reduced to 1 after it wears off, healing at half rate until recovered).</li> <li>Munificent Antivenin (2/3; a universal antivenin that makes the user &quot;painfully inactive&quot; for a few ticks).</li> <li>Philtre of Desire (2/2; one makes you better at social stuff against one specific target when imbibed, another lowers the drinker's MDV).</li> <li>Tiger's Heart Elixir (2/3; +1 to Valor; other versions boost other Virtues).</li> <li>Valiant Warrior Formula (2/2; turns an Extra into a Heroic Mortal).</li> <li>Deathlord's Breath (3/4; works better than salt as a undead ward, but a deadly poison to the living that makes those it kills into zombies and hungry ghosts).</li> <li>8-Scream Devil Powder (3/4; WotLA item, inflicts -4 pain penalty until scrubbed off).</li> <li>Seven Bounties Paste (3/4; core rules in 2nd, Arms of the Chosen in 3rd).</li> <li>Sweet Cordial (3/4; core rules in 2nd, Arms of the Chosen in 3rd).</li> <li>Wind-Fire Potion (3/4; +1 die to physical attributes/Valor/Wits, -1 dot to Compassion/Temperance/Intelligence, gives heroic mortals two -4 health levels, addictive).</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T12:30:41-07:00","id":1247778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do?p=1247291#post1247291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if you do stuff like put it and sell it on the market? I mean, its not just for the PCs, its also for worldbuilding.</div> </div> </div> </div>PCs and NPCs don't evolve by the same logic.<br /> Choose your poison: free, xp-less upgrades or a half-cosmetic half-narrative excuse to buy upgrades?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T19:43:36-07:00","id":1247876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245145-what-can-potions-and-ointments-in-2e-3e-do?p=1247778#post1247778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PCs and NPCs don't evolve by the same logic.<br /> Choose your poison: free, xp-less upgrades or a half-cosmetic half-narrative excuse to buy upgrades?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good god, all I wanted to do was worldbuild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":